namespace Ghul is
    // Implemented by a type that can be shown in a medium other than text:
    // an image, a document, a chart. A host that shows values - a notebook,
    // a REPL, the playground - can show one of these in place of the text.
    //
    // Displayable customises the text `$` and `inspect` produce for a
    // value. Renderable offers other media for the same value, which a
    // host can show in place of that text.
    //
    // Give each representation as a MIME type and its content, best
    // first. Text formats are UTF-8. The host chooses which MIME types it
    // honours and uses the first it does; a type implementing this cannot
    // rely on any particular one being shown, and the text `$` writes is
    // always there as the fallback.
    //
    // A host that shows output in a web page must not insert text/html or
    // image/svg+xml from a value into its own document: either can carry
    // script. Such a host shows raster image types only, as a data URL
    // inside a sandboxed frame, or skips the representation.
    //
    // Open because a type chooses its representations by implementing
    // this, which downstream assemblies have to be able to do.
    trait Renderable open is
        representations() -> Collections.Iterable[(mime: string, content: ubyte[])] pure
    si
si
